#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# SERVE THE 3D PAGE -- a projected scene and a terminal -- over TLS.
#
#     cd modules/RenderProvider/scripts && etcs serve_scene3d.etcs
#     then open https://localhost:8443/
#
# RUN IT FROM THIS DIRECTORY. Every path below is relative to it. Same shape as
# PaintProvider's serve_paint.etcs, and for the same reasons: one FileHtmlPage
# child (two StaticHtmlPage siblings under one server is a coin flip the hash
# re-tosses), the two isolation headers without which a -pthread build's Workers
# die on `wasmMemory is undefined`, and every script MOUNTED at the path it is
# fetched from rather than copied into www/.
#
# ONE SERVER AT A TIME on 8443. This page and the paint page are two views of
# the same runtime, not two services.

spawn NetworkProvider::HttpServer web
web.SetPort(8443)
web.EnableTLS(/tmp/etcs-cert.pem /tmp/etcs-key.pem)

# Cross-origin isolation, which is what makes SharedArrayBuffer -- and therefore
# threads -- available at all. Confirm from the page's console with
# `crossOriginIsolated, typeof SharedArrayBuffer`: true / "function".
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy same-origin)
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy require-corp)

web.spawn(NetworkProvider::FileHtmlPage tree)
tree.LoadFromDisk(./www)
tree.SetDefaultExtension(.html)

# ── the mounts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Each at the path the page stages it under (www/modules.json), which is the path
# the OS side reads it from -- so the boot script's `detach` and `run` lines are
# spelled once for both substrates instead of twice.
#
# THE GEOMETRY IS MOUNTED, NOT COPIED. www/scene3d.etcs is the session; this one
# is the reusable scene the session runs against an anchor, and it is the same
# file the native script uses. Two names, one file, no drift.
tree.MountFile(RenderProvider/scripts/scene3d.etcs ./scene3d.etcs)
tree.MountFile(RenderProvider/scripts/render_frames.etcs ./render_frames.etcs)

# The pointer half of the look control, from the repo's own scripts rather than
# a copy of it -- the key half is stated inline by the boot script, because the
# last edge is the one that blocks.
tree.MountFile(scene3d_look.etcs ../../../scripts/scene3d_look.etcs)

# The terminal view, from ShellProvider's own page rather than a copy of it.
# Mounted at "shell", which is what index.html's iframe points at; the MIME comes
# from the disk name.
tree.MountFile(shell ../../ShellProvider/scripts/www/index.html)

# The whole served surface, which is the fastest way to catch a staging mistake:
# a name the page asks for and this does not list is a 404 waiting to happen.
tree.ListPaths()

web.Start()
web.IsStarted()
